# Study Buddy frontend review

Use this optional rule for Study Buddy frontend work. Read `AGENTS.md`,
`docs/FRONTEND_CHANGE_PROCESS.md`, the relevant installed Next.js documentation,
`docs/WEBSITE_GUIDE.md` and
`docs/DMCTN_UI_TASTE_GATE.md` before proposing implementation changes.
The user's scope and approved product decisions take precedence over generic
design presets.

## Before editing

- Inspect the actual route, shared components and current worktree.
- State the learner's task, requested outcome and checkable acceptance criteria.
- An explanation, audit or documentation request is not permission to redesign.
- Preserve concurrent work and existing branch ownership; do not stage, commit,
  merge, push, migrate shared data or deploy without appropriate authorisation.
- Keep the plan proportionate. Do not require a long design ceremony for a
  small, well-specified fix.

## Preserve the approved UI

- Keep the SB branding, existing purple/neutral palettes and system fonts.
- Preserve the approved profile avatar, notification bell and contextual icons.
- Do not restart the completed icon rollout or restore temporary design routes.
- Reuse existing components; do not introduce an unrelated design system,
  glass effects, decorative fonts or dependencies as incidental changes.
- Keep illustrations uncropped where they communicate the card's content.

## Responsive and interaction checks

- Start at 320px, then check tablet and desktop, long content and browser zoom.
- Product navigation changes at 1110px; progress carousels change at 769px.
  Do not replace these with a generic shared mobile breakpoint.
- Preserve bottom-navigation clearance and device safe-area spacing.
- Check loading, empty, validation-error, retry, success and unavailable states.
- Check keyboard focus, field labels, icon-only names, reduced motion, readable
  text and touch targets. Do not infer accessibility conformance from tokens.
- Keep wide formulas, code and tables scrollable within their containers.
- The shared shell owns the page-content main landmark; do not nest another.

## Verification and handoff

Use the detailed UI checklist for relevant tests and browser checks. Separate
source inspection, automated results and live verification; a passing build is
not a browser or deployment test. Report what was not tested.
Update the relevant guides and `docs/FRONTEND_BUG_AND_FIX_HISTORY.md` for fixes.
Follow the agreed feature-branch-to-staging workflow when authorised; Git
staging and commits remain user-owned unless delegated. Production approval
is separate from staging acceptance.

Use synthetic learners and study content. Do not read environment secrets for
ordinary UI documentation, publish real recovery links, copy personal account
screens into evidence, or disclose sensitive operational findings. Follow
`SECURITY.md` for private reporting.

Summarise outcomes and remaining work in the response. Do not create public
evidence files, screenshots or temporary routes unless requested.
